@startuml sd-06-cancel-failure-delete
!include ../_style/cue.iuml
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.2
autonumber "<b>00"
title SD-6  Cancellation, worker loss and deletion — state consistency (FR-07, FR-09, NFR-03, NFR-05)
participant "React SPA" as SPA #E3F0FB
participant "FastAPI" as API #E6F4EA
database "PostgreSQL" as DB #FFF4DB
participant "GPU worker" as W #F1E8FB
participant "Maintenance" as MT #E6F4EA
participant "Media store" as MS #FFF4DB

== A  Cancel (decision D-02) ==
SPA -> API : POST /jobs/{id}/cancel
API -> DB : UPDATE status=cancelled, finished_at=clock_timestamp()\nWHERE id AND owner_id=me AND status IN (queued, running)
alt 1 row updated
  DB --> API : ok
  API --> SPA : 200 cancelled
  W -> DB : heartbeat UPDATE ... WHERE status=running AND locked_by=me
  DB --> W : 0 rows
  W -> W : abort inference, discard partial output
else 0 rows (already done, failed or cancelled; or foreign)
  API --> SPA : 409 with current status / 404 if foreign
end
note over W, DB : If the worker finishes at the same moment:\nits conditional UPDATE returns 0 rows, ROLLBACK, MP4 deleted.\nExactly one of the two UPDATEs wins (tested 40x).

== B  Worker lost ==
W -x W : process crashes / host loses power
MT -> DB : UPDATE status=failed, error_code=worker_lost\nWHERE status=running AND heartbeat_at < clock_timestamp() - threshold
DB --> MT : reaped job ids
SPA -> API : poll GET /jobs/{id}
API --> SPA : failed + clear message (no automatic retry)
opt the "dead" worker was only stalled
  W -> DB : completion UPDATE ... WHERE status=running AND locked_by=me
  DB --> W : 0 rows -> ROLLBACK, delete its MP4
end

== C  Delete an animation (FR-09, NFR-05) ==
SPA -> API : DELETE /jobs/{id}
activate API
API -> DB : SELECT status WHERE id AND owner_id=me
alt foreign or missing
  API --> SPA : 404
else status is queued or running (decision D-03)
  API --> SPA : 409 "Cancel the generation first"
else terminal state (done, failed, cancelled)
  API -> DB : BEGIN
  API -> DB : DELETE animation_job WHERE id AND owner_id RETURNING asset ids
  API -> DB : DELETE media_asset WHERE id IN (...) RETURNING storage_key
  API -> DB : COMMIT
  API --> SPA : 204
  API -> MS : delete files (after commit)
  note right of MS : A failed file delete leaves an orphan;\nthe sweeper removes it. The record is already gone.
end
deactivate API
@enduml
